The minimum is achieved by pairing $(2,3)$ (Type A: $f(2)=3,\;f(3)=4$), pairing $5$ with $7$ ($f(5)=7$), and pairing $67$ with $11$ ($f(67)=11$), all remaining primes paired arbitrarily. This is a valid $f$ by Step 3.

**Verification of the construction:** $f(f(2))=f(3)=4=2^2$ ✓; $f(f(3))=f(4)=f(2)^2=9=3^2$ ✓; $f(f(5))=f(7)=5^2$ ✓ (with $f(7)=25$); $f(f(67))=f(11)=67^2$ ✓. Complete multiplicativity gives $f(mf(n))=f(m)f(f(n))=n^2 f(m)$ ✓.

